    {
      "id": "60c680cb",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 模数转换\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3635f229",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## **AnyMath**混合信号模型\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5aafef67",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**混合信号模型** （或**混合模型**）是一种由连续时域和离散时间子系统相互连接而成的模型。信号通过**离散化**过程从连续时域子系统传输到离散时间子系统。\n\n当模型处理经过量化器处理的离散时间信号时，该信号便成为数字信号。该过程称为**模拟-数字转换**。同样，被称为**数字-模拟转换**的过程，可将数字信号转换为模拟信号。\n\n在前几节中，您进行了离散时间系统的仿真，其中模块输出是在离散时间点计算的，这些时间点由模块的采样时间分隔。仅使用差分方程（状态、输入和输出的线性组合）来计算模块输出。\n\n连续时间系统具有连续状态，因此由微分方程描述。**AnyMath**可求解这些方程，以计算任意时刻的模型状态和输出数据。\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "08ee0ffc",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 模数转换器\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "53274031",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**模数转换器（ADC）**是一种将输入模拟信号转换为离散数字编码的设备。ADC执行采样和量化操作。\n\n![4-1.jpg](attachment:4-1.jpg)\n\nADC的设计如下：\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n\n![4-2.jpg](attachment:4-2.jpg)\n\n</div>\n\n采样保持电路在开关关闭的瞬间捕获并保持其输入端的电压值。开关关闭的瞬间由主时钟决定，其频率决定了输出信号的采样率。输出信号被四舍五入到某个量化电平。\n\n**比较器**是最简单的单位ADC。它接受两个电压值作为输入。如果第一个输入端的电压高于第二个，则输出逻辑“1”；否则，输出逻辑“0”。如果有多个比较器，当输入信号超过一定电平时，相应的比较器会被触发。所有比较器的输出均被转换为二进制表示形式。\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {
        "4-1.jpg": {
          "image/jpeg": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"
        },
        "4-2.jpg": {
          "image/jpeg": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"
        }
      },
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "529b40b1",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### ADC规格\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c2645f75",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "*  **采样频率** （例如：$128$ kHz，$10$ MHz，$2504 MHz, $1$ GHz);\n*   **Bit depth** $n$ is a number of bits ($8$–$32$ bits). The number of quantization levels depends on the number of bits ($2^n$);\n*   **Input signal range**;\n*   **Signal-to-noise ratio** (dB);\n*   **Transfer function** is a relationship between the numerical equivalent of the output binary code and the magnitude of the input analog signal;\n*   **Non-linearity** of the ADC is a deviation of the actual transfer function from a linear one.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bc2bcb7c",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Quantization noise\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "12e154bd",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Source **of quantization noise** is limitation of the ADC bit depth. The absolute value of the rounding error depends on the ADC bit depth and the input signal range. To reduce quantization noise, the ADC bit depth must be increased.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f427811e",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Jitter\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d14e2142",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Jitter** is a phase noise caused by the instability of the ADC master oscillator during sampling. The performance of high-speed ADCs is often limited precisely by jitter.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "20d76950",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## The model of an ideal ADC\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0d3214c0",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In the following exercise, you will build a model of an ideal ADC (ignoring impairments) with a sampling rate of $100$ MHz. The input signal will be the sum of two analog sinusoids with frequencies of $20$ MHz and $22$ MHz.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5c521d72",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### ✏️任务1\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "de40de53",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Generate a signal as the sum of two sinusoids:\n\n1. Create a new model. Add the **Sine Wave** block to the model.\n2. In the block settings window, set the value of the parameter **Amplitude** to `0.25`, and **Frequency** to `2*pi*[20 22]*1e6` (rad/sec). At each simulation step, the block generates a vector containing two sine wave values with frequencies of $20$ MHz and $22$ MHz. Leave the remaining parameters at their default settings.\n3. Add the **Sum of Elements** block to the model. It is located in the  **Basic** -> **Math Operations** library. Connect the input of this block to the output of the **Sine Wave** block. This block adds the elements of the vector fed to its input, thereby generating the sum of two sine wave signals.\n\n{% cut \"<h5><span style=\"background-color: #c2ebff\">解决方案</span></h5>\" %}\n\n<center>\n\n![4-3.png](attachment:4-3.png)\n\n</center>\n\n{% endcut %}\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {
        "4-3.png": {
          "image/png": "data:image/png;base64,"
        }
      },
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3a6a5ac0",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Now you need to limit the ADC passband to a frequency of $50$ MHz using an analog lowpass filter. \n\nTo implement the filter, you will use the **Analog Filter Design** block (design and implementation of analog filters). This block is located in the **Signal Processing** -> **Filters** -> **Filter Designs** library.\n\n<center>\n\n![3 блок Analog Filter Design.png](attachment:3 блок Analog Filter Design.png)\n\n</center>\n\nThe **Analog Filter Design** block designs and implements Butterworth, Chebyshev Type I, Chebyshev Type II, Bessel or elliptic filters for various types of frequency response: \n\n* highpass filters, \n* lowpass filters,\n* bandpass filters,\n* notch filters.\n\nUse the parameters **Design method** and **Filter type** to specify the filter design and the type of frequency response. For each combination of filter design and frequency response type, the corresponding set of parameters is displayed. In particular, for a Butterworth lowpass filter, two parameters must be specified:\n\n* **Filter order**,\n* **Passband edge frequency, rad/s**.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {
        "3 блок Analog Filter Design.png": {
          "image/png": "data:image/png;base64,"
        }
      },
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5bec7f14",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### ✏️任务2\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2925208d",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Add an analog lowpass filter:\n\n1. Add an **Analog Filter Design** block to the model. Connect the input of this block to the output of the **Sum of Elements** block.\n2. In the block settings window, set the value of the parameter **Passband edge frequency, rad/s** to `2*pi*50e6` (i.e. $50$ MHz). Leave the remaining block parameters at their default values: **Design method** – `Butterworth`, **Filter type** (frequency response type) – `Lowpass`, **Filter order** – `8`.\n3. Add a **Zero-Order Hold** block to the model. It is located in the **Basic** -> **Discrete** library. This block holds the input value for the specified calculation step. Connect the input of this block to the output of the **Analog Filter Design** block.\n4. In the block settings window, set the value of the parameter **Sample time** to `1/100e6` (the reciprocal of the ADC sampling frequency).\n\n{% cut \"<h5><span style=\"background-color: #c2ebff\">解决方案</span></h5>\" %}\n\n<center>\n\n![4-4.png](attachment:4-4.png)\n\n</center>\n\n{% endcut %}\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {
        "4-4.png": {
          "image/png": "data:image/png;base64,"
        }
      },
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b5641994",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### The **Quantizer** block\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "73931ff4",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The **Quantizer** block quantizes the input signal using a quantization algorithm. It is located in the **Basic** -> **Discontinuities** library.\n\n<center>\n\n![4-5.png](attachment:4-5.png)\n\n</center>\n\n The block uses the round-to-nearest method to map signal values to quantized output values, which are determined by the **Quantization interval** parameter. A smooth input signal may take on a stepped form after the quantization.\n\nThe following equation describes the round-to-nearest method: \n\n$$y=q \\cdot \\text{round}(u/q),$$\n\nwhere $y$ is the quantized output signal, $u$ is the input signal, and $q$ is the quantization interval.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {
        "4-5.png": {
          "image/png": "data:image/png;base64,"
        }
      },
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "516e263c",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### ✏️任务3\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ab820b90",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Add a quantizer and complete the model:\n\n1. Add a **Quantizer** block to the model. Connect the input of this block to the output of the **Zero-Order Hold** block.\n2. In the block settings window, set the value of the **Quantization interval** parameter to `2^-8` (i.e. $2^{-8}$).\n3. Add a **Terminator** block to the model. Connect its input to the output of the **Quantizer** block.\n4. Log the model output signal.\n5. In the model settings window, set the simulation time to `10e-05` s and the step size to `1/1e9` (i.e. $10^{-9}$ s, which corresponds to a sampling frequency of $100$ MHz).\n6. In the model settings window, on the **Debugging** tab, in the **Information Display** section, select **Signal sampling rate** and **Highlighting**.\n7. Run the model. Plot the output signal in the frequency domain.\n\n{% cut \"<h5><span style=\"background-color: #c2ebff\">解决方案</span></h5>\" %}\n\nTne model:\n\n<center>\n\n![4-6.png](attachment:4-6.png)\n\n</center>\n\nThe symbol `Cont` denotes continuous (analog) signals, whilst the symbol `D1` denotes discrete signals.\n\nThe spectrum of the output signal:\n\n<center>\n\n![4-7.png](attachment:4-7.png)\n\n</center>\n\nTwo peaks are visible in the spectrum at frequencies of $20$ MHz and $22$ MHz.\n\n{% endcut %}\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {
        "4-6.png": {
          "image/png": "data:image/png;base64,"
        },
        "4-7.png": {
          "image/png": "data:image/png;base64,"
        }
      },
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b2ca720d",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### The ADC model with impairments\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4fdd1239",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Next, you will introduce three impairments into the ideal ADC model:\n\n1. Aperture jitter.\n2. Nonlinearity in the relationship between the input and output signals.\n3. Saturation of the quantizer output signal. The **Quantizer** block determines only the quantization interval size and does not limit the signal range. In practice, ADCs reach saturation when their input signals exceed certain upper and lower limits.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "599d5906",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Adding aperture jitter\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a164f81c",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Since the **Zero-Order Hold** block always samples the input data at a specific moment in time, aperture jitter is simulated by shifting the input data using the **Variable Time Delay** block. This block runs a delay on the input signal for a variable time interval. The output at the current time step is equal to the value of its input at the previous time step. This step represents the current simulation time $t$ minus the delay time $\\tau(t)$, as specified via the time delay inport.\n\n<center>\n\n![3 блок Переменное временное запаздывание.png](attachment:3 блок Переменное временное запаздывание.png)\n\n</center>\n\nA random signal, generated by the **Uniform Random Number** block, is applied to the time delay inport. The maximum jitter frequency is limited by an analog lowpass filter implemented by the **Analog Filter Design** block.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {
        "3 блок Переменное временное запаздывание.png": {
          "image/png": "data:image/png;base64,"
        }
      },
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a8226b14",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### ✏️任务4\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Название секции",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "81475cdf",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Add the aperture jitter:\n\n1. Open the model `ADC_Start.engee`.\n\n<center>\n\n![4-8.png](attachment:4-8.png)\n\n</center>\n\n2. Add the following blocks to the model:\n    * **Uniform Random Number** (**Basic** -> **Sources** library),\n    * **Analog Filter Design** (**Signal Processing** -> **Filters** -> **Filter Designs** library),\n    * **Variable Time Delay** (**Basic** -> **Continuous** library).\n\n3. Connect these blocks as shown in the figure:\n\n<center>\n\n![4-9.png](attachment:4-9.png)\n\n</center>\n\n4. In the settings windows of the **Uniform Random Number** block, set the following parameter values:\n\n<center>\n\n![4-10.png](attachment:4-10.png)\n\n</center>\n\nThus, the jitter range is from $0$ to $5 \\cdot 10^{-9}$ s.\n\n5. In the settings window of the **Analog Filter Design** block, set the following parameter values:\n\n<center>\n\n![4-11.png](attachment:4-11.png)\n\n</center>\n\nThis block limits the jitter variation frequency to $20$ MHz.\n\nLeave the block parameters of the **Variable Time Delay** block at their default settings.\n\n{% cut \"<h5><span style=\"background-color: #c2ebff\">解决方案</span></h5>\" %}\n\n<center>\n\n![4-12.png](attachment:4-12.png)\n\n</center>\n\n{% endcut %}\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {
        "4-8.png": {
